1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,832
For most of the last century, \ rich countries saw migration \ as a way out of poverty.
在上个世纪的大部分时间里， \ 富裕国家把人口迁移视为 \ 摆脱贫困的一条出路。

2
00:00:06,182 --> 00:00:11,702
A poor family moved to a better city, \ and its young people left poverty behind.
一个贫困家庭搬迁到更好的城市， \ 家里的年轻人便把贫困甩在身后。

3
00:00:12,052 --> 00:00:18,652
Recent studies \ built on income records of tens of millions of families \ tell a more complicated story.
最新的多项研究 \ 建立在数千万家庭的收入记录之上， \ 讲述了一个更为复杂的故事。

4
00:00:19,002 --> 00:00:25,602
Moving does help a poor youngster, \ the researchers report, \ but far less \ than people were once told.
搬迁确实有助于贫困年轻人， \ 研究人员报告说， \ 但幅度远小于 \ 人们曾经被告知的那样。

5
00:00:25,952 --> 00:00:31,472
The gains depend on where a family settles, \ and not on the act of leaving itself.
收益取决于一个家庭定居在何处， \ 而非取决于离开这一行为本身。

6
00:00:31,822 --> 00:00:38,734
One conclusion is uncomfortable to accept: \ a good area is not good \ because of its shops or new houses.
有一个结论令人难以接受： \ 一个好的区域之所以好 \ 并非因为那里的商店或新房子。

7
00:00:39,084 --> 00:00:47,700
It is good because of the steady groups that meet there: \ unions, clubs, two-parent homes, \ employers who keep the same staff for years.
它之所以好是因为在那里定期聚会的稳定群体： \ 工会、俱乐部、双亲家庭、 \ 以及多年留用同一批员工的雇主。

8
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:54,098
Where such groups no longer meet, \ even a move made for good reasons \ repeats the old poverty.
在这些群体不再聚会的地方， \ 哪怕一次出于良好意图的搬迁 \ 也会重复旧有的贫困。

9
00:00:54,448 --> 00:01:01,240
A family enters a new neighborhood, \ but what it really finds \ is a set of expectations about who gets help.
一个家庭进入一个新的街区， \ 但它真正发现的 \ 是一整套关于谁能得到帮助的社会预期。

10
00:01:01,590 --> 00:01:06,654
The same studies record \ what numbers capture poorly: \ the cost of leaving.
这批相同的研究记录了 \ 数字难以捕捉的东西： \ 离开故土的代价。

11
00:01:07,004 --> 00:01:14,900
Experts have interviewed hundreds of migrants now in their fifties, \ and most describe a lasting sense \ of belonging to neither place.
专家访谈了数百名现年五十多岁的移民， \ 大多数人描述了一种持久的感觉—— \ 两个地方都不完全属于。

12
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:18,778
Their hometown \ has changed beyond recognition.
他们的故乡 \ 已经变化得面目全非。

13
00:01:19,128 --> 00:01:24,504
The city they chose is where they work, \ but it is rarely the place \ they picture as home.
他们所选择的城市是他们工作之地， \ 但极少会是那个地方—— \ 他们心中描绘为家园的地方。

14
00:01:24,854 --> 00:01:29,942
One man put it plainly: \ "I come from two places \ that no longer exist."
一位男士直白地说道： \ “我来自两个地方， \ 它们都已经不复存在了。”

15
00:01:30,292 --> 00:01:35,980
Researchers treat that feeling \ as a measurable loss of social support, \ not as weakness.
研究人员把那种感受对待为 \ 社会支持网络的一种可衡量的损失， \ 而非个人的软弱。

16
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:40,698
Officials often forget \ the practical importance of that finding.
政府官员们常常遗忘 \ 那个发现所具有的现实重要性。

17
00:01:41,048 --> 00:01:48,464
If attachment to a hometown is as strong as the evidence shows, \ a plan aimed only at moving people \ will keep failing.
如果对故乡的依恋真如证据所表明的那样强烈， \ 仅仅旨在把人搬迁走的规划 \ 将会持续失败。

18
00:01:48,814 --> 00:01:56,854
Improving transport, universities and hospitals in shrinking places \ does not keep people in one place, \ as critics warn.
改善收缩萎缩地区的交通、大学与医院， \ 并不会把人们固定在一个地方， \ 像批评人士所警告的那样。

19
00:01:57,204 --> 00:02:01,980
It widens the range of lives \ a person can picture \ without leaving home.
它拓宽了生活的可能范围—— \ 一个人能够去设想的生活， \ 无需离开家乡。

20
00:02:02,330 --> 00:02:08,906
When a move does happen, \ support that travels with the young person \ matters more than a grant paid at the start.
当搬迁确实发生之时， \ 伴随年轻人一同流动的支持， \ 比出发初始发放的补贴更重要。

21
00:02:09,256 --> 00:02:16,360
The plain conclusion is \ that opportunity is spread unevenly across the country, \ and that belonging is stubborn.
最朴素的结论是： \ 机会在全国范围内的分布是不均衡的， \ 并且故土归属感是极其顽固深刻的。

22
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:22,182
A generation told to "just move" \ is learning \ that place is harder to shake than a habit.
被告知“只要搬走就好”的一代人 \ 正在懂得： \ 故土印记比生活习惯更难摆脱。

23
00:02:22,532 --> 00:02:27,284
The towns people leave \ never stop raising their youngsters \ from a distance.
人们所离开的那些城镇， \ 从未停止过养育自家的孩子， \ 隔着遥远的距离。
